# {{.Module}}

A TableTheory (TypeScript) quickstart scaffold generated by `tabletheory init --lang ts`.

## What's here

- `src/main.ts` — a create/read/delete program using TableTheory against DynamoDB Local.
- `dms.yml` — the language-neutral DMS description of the `Note` model.
- `docker-compose.yml` — DynamoDB Local (no AWS account required).

## Run it (one command)

```bash
npm install
npm run smoke
```

`npm run smoke` starts DynamoDB Local and runs the program. Expected final line:

```
OK: TableTheory CRUD against DynamoDB Local succeeded
```

Equivalently:

```bash
docker compose up -d
AWS_ACCESS_KEY_ID=dummy AWS_SECRET_ACCESS_KEY=dummy AWS_REGION=us-east-1 \
  DYNAMODB_ENDPOINT=http://localhost:8000 npx tsx src/main.ts
```

## Installing the runtime

TableTheory is distributed through GitHub Releases (not npm). `package.json` pins the
release tarball. Update the URL to a different release with the version you want; see
the [getting-started guide](https://tabletheory.theorycloud.ai/) for the current version.

`@aws-sdk/client-dynamodb` is a peer dependency and is installed here as a dev dependency.

## Next steps

- Edit `dms.yml`, then regenerate a matching TypeScript model with `tabletheory gen --lang ts dms.yml`.
- Generate CDK table constructs with `tabletheory gen --cdk dms.yml`.
- Point at real AWS by unsetting `DYNAMODB_ENDPOINT` and providing AWS credentials.
